  "summary": "Dolphin GIFs over holographic seas: the ocean as club visual.",
  "description": "Seapunk was a short, sharp net-art moment (2011-2014): Tumblr-centric visuals of CG dolphins, pixelated waves, wireframe shells and holographic gradients fused with club music (Zombelle, Ultrademon's \"seapunk\" tracks), seeded by artists around the Albertine Osteria blog and ignited when Twitter users spoofed its format into memes. Its palette — aquarium teal, hologram iridescence, sunbleached coral — and its dolphin Y2K nostalgia anticipated vaporwave's mass bloom; Rihanna's SNL appearance (2012) borrowed its graphics and caused scene controversy. As a style it belongs to the net-native family that treats the ocean as screen-saver sublime: water as CRT glow.",
  "culturalContext": "Seapunk was a 2011-2014 net-art moment: CG dolphins, wireframe waves and holographic gradients fused with club music, anticipating vaporwave; Rihanna's 2012 SNL borrowing caused scene controversy, and its aquarium-teal palette survives in Y2K revival design.",
